          "stage": "final",
          "status": "succeeded",
          "verdict": "block",
          "summary": "The analysis is incomplete for a final review stage. Critical information is missing: confidence intervals or measures of uncertainty for the cumulative incidence estimates, sample sizes per treatment group, number of events (target and competing) per group, time horizon for the reported estimates, and quantification of missingness. Without these, the reported results cannot be interpreted reliably, and reproducibility is compromised because the underlying data and curve data are not accessible. The manuscript's claim of 'interpretable local evidence' is undermined by these gaps.",
          "findings": [
            {
              "id": "F1",
              "severity": "blocker",
              "category": "reporting",
              "title": "Missing uncertainty measures for cumulative incidence estimates",
              "evidenceRefs": [
                "manuscript.md (Results section: only final cumulative incidence values given)",
                "stats-run/stats-run.json (estimates only one value per group, no standard errors or confidence intervals)"
              ],
              "whyItMatters": "Without confidence intervals or standard errors, the precision of the estimates is unknown, making it impossible to assess whether the observed difference (0.57 vs 0.89) is statistically reliable or could be due to sampling variability. This prevents any meaningful scientific interpretation.",
              "actionableFix": "Re-run the Aalen-Johansen method with pointwise confidence intervals at specified time points (or provide the full covariance function). Report 95% CIs for each group and possibly a test for equality (e.g., Gray's test). Store these in the estimates output and include in the manuscript.",
              "reentryPoint": "execution",
              "deterministicVerification": "Check that the stats-run.json or a companion file now contains an 'estimates' array with fields like 'final_cumulative_incidence', 'ci_lower', 'ci_upper', and that these values are consistent with the sample size and event counts.",
              "confidence": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "F2",
              "severity": "blocker",
              "category": "reporting",
              "title": "Missing group sizes and event counts",
              "evidenceRefs": [
                "manuscript.md (cohort construction mentions complete-case N=240 but no breakdown)",
                "stats-run/stats-run.json (rowCount=240, no per-group counts)"
              ],
              "whyItMatters": "The reliability of the cumulative incidence estimates depends on the number at risk and number of events of each type in each treatment group. Imbalance or small numbers could yield unstable estimates, even if the confidence intervals are wide. Without these counts, readers cannot gauge the trustworthiness of the results.",
              "actionableFix": "Add a table summarizing the number of subjects, total follow-up time, number of target events, number of competing events, and number of censored observations for each treatment group. This should be derived from the dataset and stored in the stats-run artifacts.",
              "reentryPoint": "execution",
              "deterministicVerification": "Verify that the numbers in the table sum to 240 and are consistent with the cumulative incidence curve (e.g., that the final incidence is not based on a handful of events).",
              "confidence": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "F3",
              "severity": "major",
              "category": "reporting",
              "title": "No specification of the time horizon for reported cumulative incidence",
              "evidenceRefs": [
                "manuscript.md (Results say 'final cumulative incidence' but no time point)",
                "stats-run/stats-run.json (no time column in estimates)"
              ],
              "whyItMatters": "Cumulative incidence is a function of time; the 'final' value depends on the last observed time, which may differ between groups or be driven by a few late events. Without stating the time at which the estimate is taken, the comparison is ambiguous. Clinical interpretation requires a relevant time horizon (e.g., 1-year, 5-year).",
              "actionableFix": "Report cumulative incidences at one or more clinically meaningful time points (e.g., 1 year, 2 years) with corresponding confidence intervals. If no such horizon exists, specify the maximum follow-up time and note that the estimate is at that variable time. The analysis should also evaluate whether the proportional hazards assumption for competing risks is met if using a specific horizon.",
              "reentryPoint": "execution",
              "deterministicVerification": "In the updated estimates, confirm that each group's cumulative incidence is reported at a common time point and that the number of subjects still at risk at that time is documented.",
              "confidence": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "F4",
              "severity": "minor",
              "category": "missingness",
              "title": "No quantification of missingness or description of complete-case exclusions",
              "evidenceRefs": [
                "manuscript.md (Methods: 'complete-case sample size was 240' without further detail)"
              ],
              "whyItMatters": "The potential for selection bias depends on the amount and pattern of missing data. Without knowing how many records were excluded due to missing values and which variables were missing, the robustness of the complete-case analysis cannot be assessed.",
              "actionableFix": "Report the total number of records before exclusion, the number excluded, and the reasons (e.g., missing treatment, missing outcome, missing time). Provide a missingness table by variable. If feasible, consider sensitivity analysis for missing data.",
              "reentryPoint": "execution",
              "deterministicVerification": "Check that the reported numbers add up and that the missingness rate is not extreme (<5% might be ignorable, but >20% would be concerning).",
              "confidence": 0.9
            },
            {
              "id": "F5",
              "severity": "blocker",
              "category": "reproducibility",
              "title": "Raw data and curve data not accessible, preventing full verification",
              "evidenceRefs": [
                "manuscript.md (states 'Raw row-level data allowed: true' but data not included in artifacts)",
                "stats-run/diagnostics.json (references curve_path but the CSV is not provided)"
              ],
              "whyItMatters": "Reproducibility demands that the underlying data and all derived outputs (including the cumulative incidence curve) be available for inspection. Without them, an independent reviewer cannot confirm the calculations, check for outliers or data errors, or replicate the analysis.",
              "actionableFix": "Include the full dataset (if PHI-allowed) or a synthetic/de-identified version in the run directory artifacts. Also include the cumulative incidence CSV file referenced in diagnostics. Update the artifact inventory hash accordingly.",
              "reentryPoint": "execution",
              "deterministicVerification": "Verify that the dataset has 240 rows, columns match the variables list, and that re-running the analysis produces identical estimates. The curve CSV should have time, CIF, and CI columns for each group.",
              "confidence": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "F6",
              "severity": "minor",
              "category": "reporting",
              "title": "Vague statement about deterministic methods checks without listing specific issues",
              "evidenceRefs": [
                "manuscript.md (Methods: 'The methods review found advisory issues that need human review')"
              ],
              "whyItMatters": "The manuscript says issues were identified but does not disclose them, making it impossible for readers to assess the severity or whether the conclusions are undermined. This undermines transparency.",
              "actionableFix": "Explicitly list the advisory issues from the methods review (e.g., from stats-qa or other checks) and state how they were addressed or why they can be deferred. If no substantive issues remain, remove this boilerplate statement.",
              "reentryPoint": "qa",
              "deterministicVerification": "Check that the stats-qa.json or a separate methods review log contains no blocking warnings beyond those already noted. Cross-reference with the manuscript's limitations section.",
              "confidence": 0.8
